# Vision-routing patch for forky's src/route.ts

This patch adds image-aware routing: any request carrying an image block
(including images nested inside `tool_result.content`) is routed to a
vision-capable model over OAuth instead of the execution backend (GLM-5.2),
which has no vision capability.

As of 2026-06, this code is already merged into forky's `main` branch at
the box this skill was built on. This file exists so a fresh clone that
lacks the patch (upstream reverted, or a fork) can be brought up to par.

The install-forky.sh script checks for the `vision` reason string in
src/route.ts and only applies this patch if it's missing.

## How to apply manually

Open `src/route.ts` and make these changes:

### 1. Add `"vision"` to the RoutingDecision reason union

```diff
-  reason: "sentinel" | "opus" | "execution" | "classifier";
+  reason: "sentinel" | "opus" | "execution" | "classifier" | "vision";
```

### 2. Add the VISION_MODEL constant near the other model constants

```typescript
// The execution backend (e.g. GLM-5.2) has no vision capability, so any request
// carrying an image must be handled by a vision-capable model over OAuth.
const VISION_MODEL = process.env.FORKY_VISION_MODEL ?? "claude-opus-4-7";
```

### 3. Add the helper types and hasImageContent() function

```typescript
type MessageContentBlock = { type?: string; content?: unknown };
type RoutableBody = {
  tools?: ReadonlyArray<{ name?: string }>;
  messages?: ReadonlyArray<{ content?: unknown }>;
};

// True if any message (or any tool_result nested inside one) carries an image
// block. Claude Code delivers screenshots as `type: "image"` blocks, including
// inside `tool_result` content arrays, so we scan one level deep.
function hasImageContent(body: RoutableBody): boolean {
  const blockHasImage = (block: MessageContentBlock): boolean => {
    if (block?.type === "image") return true;
    return Array.isArray(block?.content)
      && block.content.some((b) => typeof b === "object" && b !== null && (b as MessageContentBlock).type === "image");
  };
  return (body.messages ?? []).some((m) =>
    Array.isArray(m.content)
    && m.content.some((b) => typeof b === "object" && b !== null && blockHasImage(b as MessageContentBlock)),
  );
}
```

### 4. Add the vision branch in decideRoute(), before the final execution return

```typescript
  if (hasImageContent(body)) {
    return { provider: "anthropic-oauth", rewriteModel: VISION_MODEL, reason: "vision" };
  }
```

### 5. Update decideRoute's signature to accept RoutableBody

```diff
-export function decideRoute(model: string, body: { tools?: ReadonlyArray<unknown> } = {}): RoutingDecision {
+export function decideRoute(model: string, body: RoutableBody = {}): RoutingDecision {
```

## Override

Set `FORKY_VISION_MODEL` in `~/dev/forky/.env` to use a different vision model
(defaults to `claude-opus-4-7`).
